\subsection{Malfunctioning GPU machines}
Both machines (\code{in5050-2014-11} and \code{in5050-2016-10}) were down since Friday 2025-02-31 afternoon, which is when we were both wrapping up our code optimizations, and started to collect profiling summaries for this report. This consequently affect both our code delivery, as we could not test the last commits we had planned to include, and made it impossible to add any new major optimizations.

We had planned to collect profiles for each feature of optimization we have added, but this was impossible since we do not have access to an Nvidia machine when the servers are down. We do have some data points, but we can't know for certain which commits they belong to. 

Most of this report stems from the progressive profiling we have done, and the vibes we've felt from each step. Sadly, though, we did not have a chance to make a combinatorial permutation of the different approaches, nor do we have exact values for what each step of the kernel tuning added.

